 @Facehate666     why are you so hellbent on defending what objectively just is a mediocre product? If you just judge it by the three measures, power, price and performance its almost dead last. These are the facts okay. Please read carefully. If we remove turing, Ampere is the second worst gen by performance increase. It's the worst in price/performance and it increased perf/watt by ~10% tying it with the bottom three generations here. Overall it's the worst, second worst and third worst generation of gpu that Nvidia released over the last 15 odd years. You can verify these numbers by just using Benchmark sites you trust.

So, it's not my opinion that ampere is almost dead last and a disappointment. It's just a fact.

Steve is perfectly aware which is why his conclusion was that the 3080 was basically "good enough" compared to turing. Which is hardly praise at all.

 @Facehate666  I'm not thinking in a decade ago. I'm thinking more. So long that there's a very clear pattern emerging. If you look at the numbers. Ampere is quite weak and it doesn't shift the perf/watt needle much at all. Let alone speaking price.

That's just a fact. It's not negotiable. I didn't make it up. It's not an opinion. I care about performance when I buy a GPU. Therefore I think it's a poor showing.

